    "measurementTechnique": [
      "These simulations used the E3SM Land Model (ELM) coupled to PFLOTRAN via the Alquimia interface to simulate subsurface biogeochemistry and its responses to tidal fluctuations and salinity inputs. Simulations were forced using site-specific meteorology and patterns of tidal fluctuations for the study site, a low marsh at the Plum Island Ecosystems LTER near Rowley, MA. The biogeochemical reaction network included aerobic decomposition, fermentation, sulfate reduction, iron reduction, and methanogenesis as well as iron oxide and iron sulfide mineral precipitation and dissolution. Model simulations were evaluated using eddy covariance flux measurements, soil carbon profiles, and porewater measurements from previously collected datasets (see related references)."
    ],
